  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses exclusively on the maximum outcome of each lottery and would favor Lottery B due to its higher maximum (2500 vs. 2400). However, the individual does not base their decision on which lottery offers the highest possible outcome. Instead, they acknowledge the higher outcome in B but explicitly downplay its importance ('only 100', 'not so much'). Their justification centers on risk aversion, the high probability of winning in both, and the value of certainty — not on maximizing the best possible outcome. While the maximum outcome of B is mentioned, it is not used as a deciding factor; rather, it is discounted. Therefore, the individual does not apply the decision rule of preferring the lottery with the more favorable maximum outcome. The information relevant to the reason (maximum outcomes) is acknowledged but not used in the decision logic.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
}

